- 🔴 KS-1180 — a tier-1 statusless document whose doc-level _source is originate still reports on-chain
- 🔴 KS-1180 — a tier-1 statusless document whose doc-level _source is ANCHOR_STORE still reports on-chain

## Tamper (test-only mode — the checker plants this in a clone to prove your cells can go red)

line: 703
from: `      (persistedStatus === 'confirmed' || (persistedStatus == null && (doc as any)._source !== 'anchor_store')), // KS-1073: carve-out tier-1 only; anchor-store rows are never statusless`
to: `      (persistedStatus === 'confirmed' || (persistedStatus == null && !(doc as any)._source)), // KS-1073: carve-out tier-1 only; anchor-store rows are never statusless`
statement_ok: the `from` line is the LAST conjunct of the `Boolean(` call that defines `persistedAnchored` at `:699-704`; the other three conjuncts are `:700` `persistedTxHashIsReal` (`:622-625`: a non-empty string without a `tx_sim_`/`mock_tx_`/`tx_` prefix), `:701` `persistedBlockHeightIsHeight` (`:637-640`: a positive integer) and `:702` `!persistedDeclaredSimulated` (`:642`), and for the red cells' blob `{ txHash: 'a' x 64, blockHeight: 4242 }` all three are true, so this line alone decides the value; `:704` only closes the call. `persistedStatus` is `null` (`:605`, no `status` key), so `to` reduces the line to `!(doc as any)._source`, false for `'originate'` and `'ANCHOR_STORE'`. The verdict is read at `:722-729`: `liveAnchored` is false (`:660`; the cells' `fetch` stub answers 404 because `verify` sets `liveAnchorReply = null`), `confidenceForAnchorStatus(null)` is not `'pending-onchain'` and `persistedConfidence` is undefined, so the answer is `off-chain-only`. This is the #1005 gate's GL tamper byte-for-byte on this line (`evidence/instruments/run.py:32`: `(doc as any)._source !== 'anchor_store'` → `!(doc as any)._source`).

## Output

Exactly ONE ```diff block containing ONLY the modified test file (`--- a/…` / `+++ b/…`, path repo-relative
`Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1073-tier-2-verify-has-no-statusless.test.ts`); the SEVEN hunks
exactly as the headers above say (E4 and E5 are one hunk each); blank context lines keep their leading space; correct
hunk counts. No hunk for `verification.ts`.

